{"kind":"report","text":"Checker review of the S4 repair diff from 1e36fb12 to head c7a70f9dc9886a660485c7ecb93c2a6320f6bb80, tree 4c6db559, for request a7d77a9b, ruling 4a276240 and review request adff7a68. Verdict: APPROVED.\n\nThis review covers the diff and Gate 4. The other conclusions of 2b29878c carry over, because the diff doesn't touch that code. I read the whole production diff and the new tests. I ran no second independent read, since the diff is small and answers named items.\n\n## The six items\n\n1. Omitted arguments: `service.ts:384` now passes `given`, and `read-tools.test.ts` covers it.\n2. Stale Approve: `decision.ts` `admit` now throws `ViewError(\"stale\", ...)` for a changed Question and for a failed read. `decision.test.mjs` runs the real Wire, service and Decision path, and it signs and submits nothing.\n3. Foreign comment: `matchItem` now requires a FactRef's `at` to equal the scope. A comment's FactRef must also equal the hash from the checked history, which closes a same-position wrong-hash case that I hadn't asked for.\n4. History count: `keepEntry` charges each distinct entry once, and it compares a repeat with the kept entry. The test passes at 512 and refuses 513 with `history-limit`. The misleading comment is gone. Both pages state the limit and what happens above it.\n5. Large body: `context` drops `items` and marks the current version instead of repeating its text. A 65,536-byte body now fits, with a case. A body of the same size made of characters that JSON escapes still refuses with `context-output-limit`. That refusal is stated in both pages and tested, and I accept it.\n6. Mark reason: a `ViewError` now keeps its reason, with a case that also shows the previous store bytes unchanged.\n\n## Ruling 4a276240\n\n- The limit is 512, and each entry is charged once. A history page holds 200 entries or 1 MiB (`contract/src/read.ts:33-34`), so an ordinary 512-entry lane takes three pages, well inside the limit of 16. A lane of large entries can hit `page-limit` first, and both pages say so.\n- Both pages now say that a room with more than six lanes has omissions and offers no Mark reviewed, and that a mark needs a complete collection. The old note sentence about omitted scopes is gone. Reaching those lanes stays with request ca74f78b.\n- `since` stays a pure read.\n\n## Gate 4 and checks at this head\n\n- Gate 4 at 43d918da closed 0/0 with complete capture and matching source after the run. Its `test.log` shows Node 95, Counting 56, Plain 3,202 with one skip and Native 889 with two skips.\n- From 43d918da to this head, only the note and the repair manifest change, so no new gate is due.\n- The evidence verifies. The manifest has SHA-256 894a6aab, and all 49 of its cited files match. The unit has 322 files, its `SHA256SUMS` reruns clean, and no file is writable.\n- The 42 artifacts match the 42 paths that differ from main. `git merge-tree --write-tree` onto main 112eff12 gives tree 4c6db559.\n- One seal changes, `service.ts:McpService`, which fits the one-line change.\n- I ran these once each:\n  - `s4.test.mjs` and `decision.test.mjs` pass 11 of 11;\n  - `security-entry-points.test.mjs` passes 10 of 10;\n  - `check-notes` gives 0 warnings, with the note at 40,927 bytes;\n  - `check-commit-messages` checks 27 with 0 flagged;\n  - `check-doc-links` on an export finds 775 links with 0 broken;\n  - `git diff --check` is clean.\n- The worktree stayed clean.\n\n## Points that do not block\n\n1. The whole-lane read still charges unrelated entries. A busy lane past 512 entries loses its Decision card, and both pages say so. The ruling leaves reading only the Question's entries for later, and that limit will return in a long-lived Issue.\n2. The note is within 33 bytes of the 40 KB limit, so its next addition needs a split or a trim.\n3. The real S1-room render stays owed under f152f847, and this local evidence doesn't stand in for it.\n\n## For the landing\n\nKeep the first line of the message within 100 code points, under ruling dee246b9. Workers stay at 112eff12 until the J4 witness closes, as you and the planner state.\n\n## Architecture\n\nThe repairs stay in the adapter, the MCP change is one line, and `ViewError` is the existing typed answer. Approved.\n\n## Security\n\nNo authority is added. A stale card signs nothing, a comment's attribution is now bound to the scope and the hash, and the two items from my earlier conclusion hold. Approved.\n\n## Simplification\n\n`keepEntry` replaces two separate counts, and `context` returns less. Approved.\n\n## Conclusions\n\n- Architecture: approved.\n- Security: approved.\n- Simplification: approved.\n- The request's checks: all six items, the ruling, Gate 4 and the evidence hold. This approval covers local source only. It claims no hosted, provider or S1-room result.","body":{"artifact":"git:sha1:589bca982736a2361d15d53f7572375ef2f7aaf3#git:sha1:3bab110ea8b07796be6e5594344221a9623beaf5","binding":"assigned","head":"c7a70f9dc9886a660485c7ecb93c2a6320f6bb80","head_news_acknowledged":"[\"git:sha1:589bca982736a2361d15d53f7572375ef2f7aaf3#git:sha1:de487040e41e915368b0bf24cdf5186c15244a40\"]","implementations":"[\"git:sha1:589bca982736a2361d15d53f7572375ef2f7aaf3#git:sha1:185054c48cd88f847085bf417d43df15648e1f49\"]","review_frontier":"git:sha1:589bca982736a2361d15d53f7572375ef2f7aaf3#git:sha1:de487040e41e915368b0bf24cdf5186c15244a40","review_path":"reviewguard@1","stale":"true","stale_bases":"git:sha1:589bca982736a2361d15d53f7572375ef2f7aaf3#git:sha1:03987fc1a4dd0b0740f63dd48676d212b5d60ad1, git:sha1:589bca982736a2361d15d53f7572375ef2f7aaf3#git:sha1:041b3a40d7b95f643877654924b3ce3c8689066b, git:sha1:589bca982736a2361d15d53f7572375ef2f7aaf3#git:sha1:0cac9e4e7bdcdadabe5c2116bdcd9342aa7809f1, git:sha1:589bca982736a2361d15d53f7572375ef2f7aaf3#git:sha1:1a22a30dbf1ce7e54207ec4cdf6803ab8c27fff9, git:sha1:589bca982736a2361d15d53f7572375ef2f7aaf3#git:sha1:1ae2dba84ac1553a433b02f7c1b861a832cf32dd, git:sha1:589bca982736a2361d15d53f75723